A||||2||FieroLT1||Wing studs and deck lid holes don't match||||9||
Z||000000||FieroLT1||07-24-2001||10:54 PM||||When I bought my Formula the wing had been stolen and four holes left there in bad shape. To prevent water from going in, and with no immediate desire to get another wing, I glassed the holes shot.<BR>I have now acquired a new factory wing from FieroJon, and the studs in it do not match the old holes on my deck lid. The wing has the studs about 5.75" apart and the lid had holes about 4.75" apart or about an inch shorter. This wing, however, has another set of available holes at the right distance. I have to drill new holes on the lid anyways so; What should I do? Move the studs to the right location? Or leave the studs where they are and drill the new holes so they match.<BR>One might think the farther apart the more support but... does it even matter?<BR>Anyone has gone through this before? <P>------------------<BR>Winston Ojeda<BR><B>88 Formula LT1</B><BR>Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA<BR><A HREF="http://www.FieroLT1.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.FieroLT1.com</A><BR><I>Home of the Fiero LT1</I><BR>  <A HREF="mailto:wojeda@FieroLT1.com">wojeda@FieroLT1.com</A> ||||reg||9
Z||000001||mrfiero||07-24-2001||11:09 PM||||Winston,<P>The notchbacks use the more narrow holes and the fastback uses the wider ones.  It sounds like the spoiler you got came off of a fastback originally.  <P>I personally would swap the studs to the correct holes, but that is up to you.  Just make sure there is nothing in the way on the inside of the decklid (or that it will look good or not).<P> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroLT1||07-25-2001||12:06 PM||||The studs are already at the corners so I'll just drill the new holes to match.<BR>Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Winston Ojeda<BR><B>88 Formula LT1</B><BR>Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA<BR><A HREF="http://www.FieroLT1.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.FieroLT1.com</A><BR><I>Home of the Fiero LT1</I><BR>  <A HREF="mailto:wojeda@FieroLT1.com">wojeda@FieroLT1.com</A> ||||reg||1
